.TH PACFZ 1 "2026-07-08" "pacfz 1.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pacfz \- interactive fzf\-based explorer for installed pacman packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacfz
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pacfz
snapshots
.BR pacman (8)
package metadata (via
.B pacman -Qi
and
.BR "pacman -Qqm" )
into a small SQLite cache, then presents it through an interactive
.BR fzf (1)
picker: fuzzy-search the package list on the left, and get a full
colorized metadata preview: description, dependencies, install
reason, size, licenses, and any note you've attached, on the right.
.PP
The cache builds itself automatically on first use, and rebuilds
atomically (built to a temporary file, then swapped into place), so a
refresh can never leave behind a half\-written database.
.PP
.B pacfz
shares its entire filter, sort, and search flag set with
.BR pacq (1),
its non\-interactive sibling: anything you can narrow down here, you
can also script with
.BR pacq (1).
Flags specific to the interactive picker itself (note management,
.BR fzf (1)
matching mode, preview visibility) exist only in
.BR pacfz .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Filter options
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-foreign
Only foreign (AUR / non\-repo) packages.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-orphans
Only orphan packages: installed as a dependency, and now required by
nothing. Does not consider optional\-dependency relationships; see
.B "A NOTE ON ORPHAN"
below.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-explicit
Only explicitly installed packages.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-deps
Only packages installed as a dependency.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-notadep
Only packages not required by anything.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-notoptdep
Only packages that are not an optional dependency for anything.
.TP
.B \-\-has\-note
Only packages that have a user note attached.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-note
Only packages without a user note.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIFIELD VALUE\fR, \fB\-\-field\fR \fIFIELD VALUE\fR
Only packages where
.I FIELD
matches
.IR VALUE .
Repeatable; multiple
.B \-f
conditions are AND\-combined. Matching is substring by default; see
.B \-x
below.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR \fIVALUE\fR, \fB\-\-any\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Only packages where
.I any
field matches
.IR VALUE .
Repeatable, and AND\-combined with everything else active.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exact\-match
Use exact equality instead of substring matching for
.B \-f
and
.BR \-a .
.TP
\fB\-v\fR \fR[\fIFILTER\fR]\fR, \fB\-\-invert\fR \fR[\fIFILTER\fR]
Invert results. Bare
.B \-v
inverts the entire query, applied last, as a single unit. Given a
.IR FILTER ,
.B \-v
instead inverts only that one canned filter, leaving every other
active filter in place as a precondition; repeatable. See
.B "INVERTING RESULTS"
below.
.SS Sort options
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fR[\fIFIELD\fR]\fR, \fB\-\-sort\-by\fR \fR[\fIFIELD\fR]
Sort by
.IR FIELD .
Default field is
.IR Name ;
bare
.B \-s
with no field sorts by
.IR Installed_Size .
.B \-\-size
is a synonym for this option.
.TP
.B \-\-asc
Sort ascending. Applies to whichever field is being sorted.
.TP
.B \-\-desc
Sort descending.
.SS Size
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-totalsize
Print the total installed size of exactly the packages selected by
the other active filters, not the whole system.
.SS Display options
.TP
.B \-\-exact
Use exact (not fuzzy) matching inside the
.BR fzf (1)
picker itself. This is
.BR fzf 's
own matching mode, distinct from
.B \-x
above, which affects the SQL\-level
.B \-f / \-a
filters before any results ever reach
.BR fzf .
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-notes
Hide user notes in the preview pane. The notes database is not even
opened in this mode.
.SS Notes
.TP
\fB\-D\fR \fIPKG NOTE\fR
Set
.I NOTE
as the note for package
.IR PKG .
.TP
\fB\-D\fR \fIPKG\fR \fB\-d\fR
Delete the note for package
.IR PKG .
.TP
.B \-\-notes\-list
List every package that currently has a note.
.SS Other
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-refresh
Rebuild the package cache from
.BR pacman (8)
and exit. Prints a short summary (packages inserted, foreign packages
marked) unless
.B \-\-verbose
is also given.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed pacfz version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print extra diagnostic output. For a normal search, this prints the
resolved SQL query and bound parameters to standard error before
entering
.BR fzf (1).
For
.BR \-r / \-\-refresh ,
this additionally prints INFO\-level build logs and a sample of the
packages just inserted. Not available in
.BR pacq (1).
.SH INTERACTIVE PICKER KEYS
.TP
.B ctrl\-r
Rebuild the package cache and reload the visible list without leaving
.BR fzf (1).
The header briefly shows \(lq✓ cache refreshed at HH:MM:SS\(rq
so repeated presses are visibly distinct from each other.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. This includes the case where the query matched no packages:
.B pacfz
prints \(lqNo packages found.\(rq and exits without opening
.BR fzf (1).
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: invalid flag combination, a database error, or
.BR fzf (1)
is not installed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pacfz \-m
Browse foreign packages interactively.
.TP
.B pacfz \-e \-\-desc \-\-size
Browse explicitly installed packages, largest first.
.TP
.B pacfz \-o \-k
Browse orphans that are also not an optional dependency for anything.
.TP
.B pacfz \-e \-v notadep \-v notoptdep
Browse explicitly installed packages that
.I are
required by something, optionally or not (see
.B "INVERTING RESULTS"
below).
.TP
.B pacfz \-t \-\-verbose
Print the resolved SQL query, then the total installed size of every
package.
.SH INVERTING RESULTS
Bare
.B \-v
negates everything else you specified, as one unit, applied last:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pacfz \-m \-v            # NOT foreign
.EE
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v\fR \fIFILTER\fR instead negates only that one named filter,
leaving every other active filter in place as a precondition, and is
repeatable:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pacfz \-e \-v orphan                    # explicit, and NOT an orphan
pacfz \-e \-v notadep \-v notoptdep      # explicit, and NOT
                                        # (notadep AND notoptdep)
.EE
.RE
.PP
.I FILTER
is one of
.IR foreign ", " orphan ", " explicit ", " deps ", " notadep ", "
.IR notoptdep ,
or its short letter:
.IR m / o / e / d / n / k .
.SH A NOTE ON ORPHAN
Here,
.I orphan
means: installed as a dependency, and now required by nothing
(equivalent to
.BR "pacman \-Qdt" ).
It does
.B not
consider optional\-dependency relationships, so a package that is
.I only
an optional dependency of something else still counts as an orphan.
Combine with
.B \-k
to additionally exclude those:
.BR "pacfz \-o \-k" .
.SH A NOTE ON LOCALE
.B pacfz
parses the package sizes
.B pacman -Qi
prints, and those are formatted according to the system locale.
Both a period (\(lq56.72 KiB\(rq) and a comma (\(lq56,72 KiB\(rq) are
accepted as the decimal separator. Locales that use a different
separator style for this purpose (for instance a space or apostrophe
as a thousands separator) are not supported, and a size in that form
will fail to parse during a cache rebuild. Both binary
(\fIKiB\fR, \fIMiB\fR, \fIGiB\fR, \fITiB\fR) and decimal
(\fIKB\fR, \fIMB\fR, \fIGB\fR, \fITB\fR) units are recognized, each
converted with its correct multiplier.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PACFZ_DB_PATH
Overrides the package cache DB path outright. Default:
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/pacman_packages.db .
.TP
.B PACFZ_NOTES_DB_PATH
Overrides the notes DB path outright. Default:
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/pacfz/user_data.db .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pacman_packages.db
The package metadata cache, rebuilt from
.BR pacman (8)
output. Not removed by uninstalling the package; see
.BR ENVIRONMENT
above to relocate it, or remove it by hand.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pacfz/user_data.db
Per\-package user notes. Also not removed by uninstalling the
package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacq (1),
.BR pactui (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR fzf (1)
.SH AUTHOR
marco-l
